      "message": "AI-assisted review. The two blockers are the main ones: the auto-reset restores the inherited level rather than the previous one the doc promises, and invalid `--reset-after` durations are handled inconsistently.\n\nThis patch adds no tests. Could cover the following scenarios:\n\n* with an injected/controllable scheduler (no sleeps): explicit WARN -\u003e DEBUG -\u003e WARN (incl. a different parent level)\n* inherited -\u003e DEBUG -\u003e inherited again; no-NAME restoring each logger\u0027s own previous value; a later permanent change and an explicit reset versus a pending timer (per the chosen policy)\n* a stale callback that has already started not overwriting a newer change\n* 0/empty/negative/malformed durations failing with nonzero status while 30min/2h/1day schedule",
