      "message": "Levels change here, before `schedule()` below. If scheduling is rejected (e.g. a shutting-down queue) the new levels stay installed with no reset. Roll back the captured levels and fail the command if scheduling throws, using the same synchronization as the reset registry so rollback can\u0027t overwrite a newer change. Minor, same file: compute `Level.toLevel(level.name())` once rather than per logger, and use `.toList()` instead of `.collect(Collectors.toList())` at line 91.",
