      "side": 1,
      "message": "`setLevel(null)` enables inheritance, it does not restore the previous level the doc promises (\"back to their previous level\"). With an ERROR parent and an explicit WARN logger, temporary DEBUG expires to ERROR, not WARN. Capture each logger\u0027s explicit `getLevel()` (including `null`) before changing it and restore that. Use `getLevel()`, not `getEffectiveLevel()`, so inherited loggers keep inheriting. A `HashMap\u003cLogger, Level\u003e` holds the `null` values; `Collectors.toMap`/`Map.copyOf` do not.",
